From 27ff8c731991def9708baa232cdc0c57cfeeb2d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Turquoise Bay AI <11993289+hughmadden@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 21:47:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(hostcache): evict the least recently used RAM
 snapshot first, not every prompt before any turn

The host cache evicted through Retention::evict_one_where, the device tier's
bank order: every prompt snapshot before any turn snapshot, oldest first
within a bank. A prompt snapshot shares its pages with its conversation's
turn snapshot, so deleting it frees a tail but no shared page. Under page
pressure that order deleted every prompt snapshot, the fresh ones included,
before the first stale turn snapshot, and an exact repeat of a recent prompt
(a retry, a regenerate, identical agent prompts) prefilled from cold.
Measured on a sibling engine with the same host-cache design
(hughmadden/mimo26f-afd v1.1.1): after a 64K-1M ladder, exact repeats of
130K-token prompts prefilled from cold in 37-41 s instead of restoring from
RAM in about 0.2 s.

Snapshots now stamps each snapshot with a use count at commit and at every
lookup hit (HostSnapshot::last_use, unique among resident snapshots) and
evicts the unpinned snapshot with the smallest stamp, whichever bank it is
in; at equal use a prompt snapshot goes before a turn snapshot (victim()).
Lookups still use the Retention radix and eviction still removes the victim
from it, so a host hit is still exactly a Retention hit. The device tier is
unchanged: v41_native_serve::prefix still evicts through
Retention::evict_oldest (prompts first).

One side effect of the old order is gone on purpose: commit_store's
replace-check (Radix::lookup) refreshed the radix clock of a same-bank
ancestor, which counted a store as a use of the ancestor. Now only a store
of the snapshot itself or a lookup hit on it counts as a use.

Tests: eviction_order_is_prompts_before_turns_oldest_first pinned the old
order; it is replaced by
eviction_order_is_least_recently_used_first_across_banks. New
a_fresh_prompt_snapshot_outlives_a_stale_turn_snapshot evicts two
conversations down to the newer one's footprint: the exact repeat of the
newer prompt still hits (the old order evicted it). Both fail against the old
evict_one. The HC-2/HC-5 reference model (tests/common) mirrors the new rule
and Model::check also compares last_use. ds41rt-hostcache: 219 passed, 0
failed; the two ignored HC-6 soaks pass when run explicitly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
